message: "If you use this software or the accompanying study, please cite it as below."
title: "Jev-Routed Temporal Granularity with Recovery and Hysteresis for Causal Video Generation"
abstract: >-
  Official code, locked protocols, calibration freezes, and audit artifacts for a
  hardware-conditional feasibility study of adaptive temporal granularity in causal
  video generation. Pairing a frame-wise mode (c1-1) with a chunk-3 mode (c3-3) and a
  near-zero-cost hold mode on Causal-rCM (Wan2.1-1.3B), the study audits three
  preconditions: a mode that is genuinely cheaper on the deployment hardware, a signal
  that predicts hard segments before generation, and an independent endpoint that
  certifies the trade. Routing uses the Jev System One oracle with a two-threshold
  controller with hysteresis and forced recovery. Audits run on a Tesla T4 and an
  A100-SXM4-80GB, with negative and failed experiments preserved as evidence.
